{"title":"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which statement is correct?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516a736de3ade6a1de5022db16d3b5242aeba5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } \\text{If } x&lt;0, \\text{then } x^2&gt;x. \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\text{If } x^2&gt;0, \\text{then } x&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"423\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a103b4952db5585c358e1a36f54cdc817a150fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } \\text{If } x^2&gt;x, \\text{then } x&gt;0. \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } \\text{If } x^2&gt;x, \\text{then } x&lt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"462\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7a6fb8c29da1d18d7b290d91dbb98fa41f46a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\text{If } x&lt;1, \\text{then } x^2&lt;x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by going statement by statement.\n</p><p>For (A), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80336160f9dfd806f37621fd3f604771d8a85c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> for all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bfbadb4704eded8b419033064254fefb5822fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2&gt;0&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79e0e8ce41b5c08729443bcc258d13ca061ff35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" /> is true.\n</p><p>We can give counterexamples for all other statements:\n</p><p>For (B), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>For (C), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>For (D), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>For (E), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf